   $q$Listen. A nest is a safe home for baby birds. Many birds hide their nests high in trees or deep in thick bushes. Soft grass and feathers inside the nest keep the eggs warm. The parent birds often stay close by to guard it. Some birds even build nests in holes where other animals cannot reach. Which reason supports the point that a nest is a safe home? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is hidden.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It is hidden."}},{"text":"It is brown.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It is brown."}},{"text":"It is round.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It is round."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is hidden.$q$, $q$The author says a nest is a safe home for baby birds. One reason is that many birds hide their nests high in trees or deep in bushes. The parent birds also stay close to guard it.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
