   $q$Listen. Kids should learn to cook with a grown up. Cooking teaches you how to measure and count, like adding two cups of flour. You can make a sandwich for yourself when you are hungry. You get to try new foods and spices, too. Best of all, you can share what you made with your family. Which reason supports the point that kids should learn to cook? Tap the picture.$q$, $q$[{"text":"bike","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"bike","count":1}},{"text":"kite","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"kite","count":1}},{"text":"sandwich","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"object_group","image":"sandwich","count":1}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$sandwich$q$, $q$The author says kids should learn to cook. One reason is that you can make a sandwich for yourself when you are hungry. Cooking also teaches you to measure.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
