   $q$Listen. A crab has a body that helps keep it safe. A hard shell covers its back like a suit of armor. Two strong claws can pinch an animal that comes too close. Many crabs can quickly hide in the sand or under rocks when danger is near. Some crabs even have colors that blend in with the sand. Which reason supports the point that a crab's body keeps it safe? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"It can swim.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It can swim."}},{"text":"It has many legs.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It has many legs."}},{"text":"It has a hard shell.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It has a hard shell."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It has a hard shell.$q$, $q$Crabs do have many legs, and some can swim, but the author does not say so. One reason the author gives is that a hard shell covers a crab's back like armor.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
