   $q$Listen. A bus is a good way to get to school. One bus can carry many kids, so there are fewer cars on the road and less traffic. Walking to school is good, too. Walking gives your body exercise, and you can wave to your neighbors on the way. You also get to enjoy the fresh air. The author says you can wave to your neighbors. Which point does that reason support? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Walking is good.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Walking is good."}},{"text":"A bus is good.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"A bus is good."}},{"text":"Cars are fast.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Cars are fast."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Walking is good.$q$, $q$Waving to your neighbors is a reason that walking to school is good. Fewer cars on the road is a reason that a bus is good.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
