   $q$Listen. Some monkeys are very clever animals. Some monkeys use rocks to crack open hard nuts so they can eat the inside. Some use sticks to poke into holes for bugs. Young monkeys often learn new tricks by watching older monkeys and copying them. That is a lot like how kids learn from grown ups. Which is NOT a reason the author gives? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"They have tails.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They have tails."}},{"text":"They watch others.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They watch others."}},{"text":"They use rocks.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They use rocks."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They have tails.$q$, $q$Monkeys have tails, but the author does not give that as a reason. The reasons are that some monkeys use rocks and sticks, and young monkeys learn by watching.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
