   $q$Listen. Bats are helpful to farmers. Many bats eat lots of bugs at night, including bugs that would munch on crops. Bats can also find their way in the dark. They make high sounds and listen for the echoes that bounce back. The echoes tell them where things are, even trees and bugs. The author says bats listen for echoes. Which point does that reason support? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Bats find their way.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Bats find their way."}},{"text":"Bats help farmers.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Bats help farmers."}},{"text":"Bats sleep all day.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Bats sleep all day."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Bats find their way.$q$, $q$Listening for echoes helps bats find their way in the dark. Eating bugs that munch on crops is the reason bats help farmers.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
