   $q$Listen. Recycling is good for the earth. Old cans and bottles can be melted down and made into new things. Recycling means less trash goes into big trash piles called landfills. It also saves trees, because old paper can be made into new paper. Even an old box can become a new one. Which reason supports the point that recycling is good for the earth? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is easy.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It is easy."}},{"text":"It saves trees.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It saves trees."}},{"text":"It is fun.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"It is fun."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It saves trees.$q$, $q$Recycling can be fun and easy, but the author does not say so. One reason the author gives is that recycling saves trees, because old paper becomes new paper.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
