   $q$Listen. Lions are strong hunters because they work as a team. Lions live in family groups called prides. The lionesses often hunt together, with some chasing and some waiting to pounce. A team can catch a big animal, like a zebra, that one lion could not catch alone. After the hunt, the pride shares the meal. Which reason supports the point that lions work as a team? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"They hunt together.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They hunt together."}},{"text":"They nap a lot.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They nap a lot."}},{"text":"They roar loudly.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"They roar loudly."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They hunt together.$q$, $q$Lions do roar, and they nap a lot, but those are not the reasons given. The author says lionesses often hunt together, so the team can catch big animals.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
