   $q$Listen. Every class should grow plants from seeds. Kids can watch a tiny seed crack open and turn into a plant. Taking care of a plant each day teaches kids to be responsible. Kids can also measure how tall the plant grows each week and make a chart. Plants can make a classroom look cheerful, too. Which reason supports the point that every class should grow plants? Tap the words.$q$, $q$[{"text":"Plants smell nice.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Plants smell nice."}},{"text":"Plants are green.","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Plants are green."}},{"text":"Kids can measure.","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Kids can measure."}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kids can measure.$q$, $q$Many plants are green, and some smell nice, but the author does not say so. One reason given is that kids can measure how tall the plant grows each week.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
