   $q$Listen. A volcano is an opening in the ground where hot, melted rock can come out. Deep under the ground, it is hot enough to melt rock. When the melted rock spills out, it is called lava. Lava cools and turns into hard rock. Over many years, this can build a mountain. What question does this text answer? Tap the question.$q$, $q$[{"text":"When will it erupt?","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"When will it erupt?"}},{"text":"What is a volcano?","is_correct":true,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"What is a volcano?"}},{"text":"Which is the biggest?","is_correct":false,"tile":{"kind":"word","value":"Which is the biggest?"}}]$q$::jsonb, $q$What is a volcano?$q$, $q$The text tells what a volcano is and how lava comes out and cools. It answers the question: what is a volcano? It does not say when one will erupt or which is biggest.$q$, 'draft', null, 'audio_picture', null)
